to teach in this old building in London  it was like a former hospital so it was  like the sort of place where you would  set a horror film  this creepy place and I remember  teaching in one of the rooms up in the  top of the building in like these low  ceilings and this kind of dusty  atmosphere I was writing on the board it  was an old crappy old whiteboard and it  was really scratchy and rubbish and also  the wall all around it was really filthy  anyway I was teaching the students  desperately trying to help them learn  English they were all peering through  the darkness to try and actually see the  things I was writing at one point the  whole board just came off the wall and  clattered onto the floor which was a  little embarrassing to say the least now  I tried to carry on you know I lent the  the board up against the wall to keep  going but it didn't work he kept  slipping down so at that point I was  like well what am I going to do how am I  gonna teach these people English on the  wall where the board had been there was  like this empty white space the only  clean part of the wall the paint was  like kind of glossy paint and I realized  that I could just write on the wall and  it was actually better than the board  had been so I just carried on writing  directly onto the wall that was an  interesting experience
 

